        "original_id": "5f48ae13-b723-5f38-b0d2-0473e703dfa0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1964–65 European Cup Winners' Cup, 1966 FIFA World Cup\n- Organizations: West Ham United, 1860 Munich, England national football team\n- People: Bobby Moore, Geoff Hurst, Martin Peters, Pelé\n- Places: Wembley Stadium\n- Concepts: football honors, defensive greatness\n\nFacts:\n- The 1964–65 European Cup Winners' Cup was won by West Ham United in a final at Wembley Stadium against 1860 Munich.\n- In the 1964–65 European Cup Winners' Cup final season, Bobby Moore captained West Ham United, and the side also included Geoff Hurst and Martin Peters.\n- One season later, Bobby Moore, Geoff Hurst, and Martin Peters starred for England in its 1966 World Cup-winning team.\n- Bobby Moore is widely regarded as one of the greatest defenders of all time.\n- Pelé said that Bobby Moore was the greatest defender he had ever played against.",
